---
kind: scene
id: hearth.firstReturn
title: The Hearth, after the first fall
components: [../../components/hearth-fire.component.lute]
on: hubVisit
priority: 90
once: user
when: 'user.runs == 1 && @cameBackFromFall'
---

## Warm stone again

::bg{location="hearth" time="night"}
@narrator{code="0010"}: Warm stone. Ash. The same crack in the ceiling she counted before she climbed.
::use{component="hearthFire" flare="low" instance="use-001"}
@maud{code="0010" emotion="warm"}: Told you. Right where you started, and the kettle's hardly cooled.
@wren{code="0010" mono}: I felt it. I felt all of it.
<match on="prev.run.fellTo">
  <when is="cinderhound">
    @maud{code="0020" emotion="guarded"}: The hounds, was it? They go for the ankles. Everyone forgets the ankles.
  </when>
  <when is="ashwraith">
    @maud{code="0030" emotion="guarded"}: A wraith. You've got that grey look. It fades.
  </when>
  <when is="gatekeeper">
    @maud{code="0040" emotion="grim"}: The Gatekeeper, on your first climb? Brave, or lost. Same thing down here.
  </when>
  <otherwise>
    @maud{code="0080"}: Whatever it was, it's behind you now. Below you, I mean.
  </otherwise>
</match>
@maud{code="0050"}: Floor {{prev.run.floor}}. Not bad for someone who didn't know which way was up.

<branch id="howAreYou" prompt="Maud waits.">
  <choice id="angry" label="Why does it keep me?">
    @maud{code="0060" emotion="wry"}: If I knew that, love, I'd have left years ago.
  </choice>
  <choice id="thanks" label="Thank you for waiting.">
    ::set{user.bond.maud += 1}
    @maud{code="0070" emotion="fond"}: Waiting's the one thing I'm good at. Go and be good at something else.
  </choice>
</branch>
